(_dative_ _plural_ - σεβέοις {{Refs|“IG” 5(1).1390.5 (from Andania))}}, (σέβω) **pious, religious**, opposed to δυσσεβής (which see), {{Refs 6th c.BC+|6th c.BC: Theognis Elegiacus 1141, 5th c.BC: Herodotus Historicus 2.141, 5th c.BC: Pindarus Lyricus “O.” 3.41; τρόπος 5th-6th c.BC: Aristophanes Comicus “Ranae” 457 (Lyric poetry)}}: not common in early Prose, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th c.BC: Gorgias Rhetor et Sophista “fragment” 6D., 5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Philebus” 39e}}; **dutiful**, especially **discharging sacred duties**, πρός or ἔς τινα, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Supplices” 340, 5th c.BC: Euripides Tragicus “Electra” 253}}; ἀνὴρ εὐ. (variant{εὐλαβής}) κατὰ τὸν νόμον {{NT|NT.Act.22.12; εὐ. καὶ φοβούμενος τὸν θεόν [prev. work] 10.2: with _accusative_ modi, -εστέρα χεῖρα}} **more righteous** in act, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|4th-5th c.BC: Aeschylus Tragicus “Choephori” 141; εὐσεβεῖς κἀξ εὐσεβῶν βλαστόντας 5th c.BC: Sophocles Tragicus “Electra” 589}}; ὁ τῶν εὐσεβῶν χῶρος, of a place in the nether world, {{Refs 5th c.BC+|5th-6th c.BC: Plato Philosophus “Axiochus” 371c}}; ἐν εὐσεβέων (i.e. χώρῳ) {{Refs 3rd c.BC+|3rd c.BC: Callimachus Epicus “Epigrammata” 12, compare “Sammelb.” 2048 (ii b.c.).}}
**b** Astrology texts, αἱ τῶν εὐσεβῶν μοῖραι {{Refs|“Catalogus Codicum Astrologorum” 8(4).227.}}
**2** as epithet of Emperors, = **Pius,** {{Refs 3rd c.AD+|Inscriptiones Graecae ad res Romanas pertinentes 3.91 (3rd c.AD), +others, “PGrenf.” 1.49.28 (3rd c.AD), “PHamb.” 1.13.2 (3rd c.AD), etc.}}; especially of Antoninus Pius, {{Refs|“IGRom.” 3.1293, +others}}
